  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We already know the critical points of the function:\n\n$$\nx=-1,\\,x=3.\n$$\n\nSince $x=-1$ does not belong to the interval $[0,5]$, the critical points on the interval $[0,5]$ are $x=3,$ and the endpoints $x=0$ and $x=5$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =-2(0)^{3}+6(0)^{2}+18(0)=0 \\\\ f(3) & =-2(3)^{3}+6(3)^{2}+18(3)=54 \\\\ f(5) & =-2(5)^{3}+6(5)^{2}+18(5)=-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step 2.\n\n* The greatest value is $f(3)=54,$ so the global maximum is ${f}_{max}=54.$\n\n* The smallest value is $f(5)=-10,$ so the global minimum is ${f}_{min}=-10.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
